{"kind":"assert","text":"H2 proof inventory (d3128559): approved as proposed.\n1. `position` and the terminal input's resolution or expiry reference retain no foreign bytes. Each charges only its own bytes inside the sealed entry. Replay resolves those facts from the order scope's own journal and answers `missing-dependency` when it is absent (sequenced note, the replay paragraph after 5.5). A member never keeps a local copy of an allocation, resolution or expiry entry.\n2. An order entry that the scope does retain, through `uses`, charges as an entry plus its possible birth, deduplicated across retained keys.\n3. The prepare quotes 2E for the observed order head, and 2E for each declared cut proof that the head does not already cover, plus the declared page bound.\n4. H4 and H6 name no local use of allocation, resolution or expiry bytes. A later need for one is a new charge and needs its own ruling before it ships; record that as an H4 open point in the H2 note amendment.\nWith this, the selected-form quote is complete on the member side; the order-side quote still waits for H3's validated order definition.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}